    "author_association": "NONE",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.ai\n\n### Description\n\nHi there, thanks for the amazing plugins! I've recently been looking into using mini.ai's textobject search to automatically generate targets for [leap-spooky](https://github.com/ggandor/leap-spooky.nvim). However I've noticed that some text objects I was expecting to be there do not exist.\r\n\r\nHere is the full list of 'builtin' ones according to the source I have:\r\n![image](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/11911259/224137247-6217db71-2463-4f0e-bac3-441db1a4abb1.png)\r\n\r\nI was just wondering what the reason is for the ommission of `w` (word), `W` (WORD) and `p` (paragraph)? And if it makes sense to add them in?",
    "closed_at": "2023-03-09T20:03:30Z",
